From: c-drew <101952850+c-drew@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:20:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] LodBridge: native chunk slots for LoD terrain after the
 vanilla grid

LodBridge reserves 4096 extra native chunk slots after the vanilla grid and lets a LoD
provider submit or clear meshes in them through the same path vanilla chunks use
(ChunkProxy.submitGeometry, factored out of rebuildSingle). The Radiance build of Voxy feeds
it; any LoD source that produces PBRVertexConsumer quads can. PBRVertexConsumer.setGlintUV
carries the LoD voxel size for per-block texture tiling in the shaders.

